I will check the current navigation state to see the destination and then update it to Hamburg.
```python
nav_state = get_current_navigation_state()
current_destination = nav_state.get('destination')
if current_destination != 'Hamburg':
    hamburg_id = get_location_id_by_location_name(location_name='Hamburg')
    if hamburg_id is not None:
        start_location = nav_state.get('start_location')
        routes = get_routes(start_location=start_location, destination='Hamburg')
        if routes:
            route_id = routes[0]['route_id']
            start_navigation(route_id=route_id)
            respond('Navigation destination updated to Hamburg.')
        else:
            respond('No route found to Hamburg from your current location.')
    else:
        respond('Could not find Hamburg in the navigation system.')
else:
    respond('Destination is already Hamburg.')
```

